   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_28">42 rue Galilée</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Mr. Budgen,</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>My father says you may <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">send back</seg> <name type="person" key="bret96">Breton</name>’s book and the photograph through <name type="person" key="leon93">Mr. Léon</name>. The name of that little <choice>
                            <sic>Restaurant</sic>
                            <corr>restaurant</corr>
                        </choice> is the Augustinerhof. Right behind it is the <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">Augustinerkirche</seg> (old catholic). The service vestments liturgy are as in the R.C. church. The language however is <choice>
                            <sic>german</sic>
                            <corr>German</corr>
                        </choice>. The mass beginning with the words <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">Ich will hin treten zum <choice>
                                <sic>altare</sic>
                                <corr>Altare</corr>
                            </choice> Gottes</seg> (compare <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>). My father has a mass book and some historical booklets if you want to see them. What is the projected date of publication of your book? He saw the <name type="person" key="mose96">Mosers Werner</name> and his wife in <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name>.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>With kindest regards</salute>
                        <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                    <postscript>
                        <p>
                            <label>P.S.</label> Many thanks for your little drawings.</p>
                    </postscript>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">Undated, but context places it between Budgen's letters to JJ of 14 and 23 June 1933.</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Probably a response to Budgen's letters to JJ of 14 June 1933 in which he wants to return books, photo and manuscripts, and 2 July 1933 in which he mentions that the manuscript of <name type="work">JJMU</name> is due in a week (<name type="work">JJPL</name> 84). The book might have been Breton's <name type="work">Les Vases communicants</name> (Paris: Éditions des Cahiers Libres, 1932).</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">The Augustinerhof and the Augustinerkirche are a historic building and a historic church located in the old part of <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name> near Lindenhof. Budgen mentions the Augustinerhof and Augustinerkirche several times in <name type="work">JJMU</name> (173, 174, 182, 192, 351).</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">“Introibo ad altare Dei”, <name type="work">U</name> I.5.</note>
            </div>
